  "sex": "4F, 4M",
  "height_cm": null,
  "weight_kg": null
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Static, upright, unconstrained T1-T12 spine with rib cage; T1 and T12 potted (Bondo), T12 bolted to horizontal surface, T1 free; follower load 0/200/400/600 N via bilateral cables through rods in T3-T11 vertebral bodies (half the load hung on each cable, pulleys below T11). No applied moment. Test order: intact rib cage -> stiffened rib cage (plates bridging costal cartilage/sternocostal joints ribs 2-5) -> ribs cut lateral to costotransverse joints (No Ribs). IDP: Gaeltec side-mounted transducer on 1.3 mm needle in the centre of the nucleus of T4-T5 and T8-T9 (radiograph-confirmed), 10 Hz, averaged static value; absolute pressure.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model T1-T12 with rib cage per condition; fix T12, T1 free.",
   "Apply follower load 0-600 N along the curvature (no moment).",
   "Report sagittal (kyphosis) angle overall T1-T12, regionally (T1-T4, T4-T8, T8-T12) and at T1-T2, T4-T5, T8-T9, T11-T12 (positive = flexed/kyphotic), as intercept at 0 N and change per kN."
  ],
  "subject_model": null,
  "notes": "Authors state testing order (intact always first) likely confounds rib-cage effects; pressure-follower slope 1.24 kPa/N (T4-T5) and 1.00 kPa/N (T8-T9) intact (Table 1). No Ribs T4-T5 at 0 N recorded as 0 kPa (at/below sensor minimum) in all specimens (text)."
 },
